--expect
55546609842069635 91823359525 10
--expect-why
DERIVED BY WALKING THE FIXTURE BY HAND. subject = [97, 223, 233, 912] = 'a',
sharp-s, 'e-acute', and U+0390. The probe's `case_map` is a binary search over
the runs the fixture supplies, `full_index` answers a row for sharp s and
U+0390 WHEN UPCASING ONLY, and `sink_string` folds the BYTES the walk emitted
with `h = h*31 + b` from 0.

UPCASING. up = [[97 122 -32 1] [224 246 -32 1]], and CASE_FULL rows 0 and 3.

  97   full_index -1, in run 0, stride 1  -> 97 - 32  =  65   'A'
  223  full_index 0   -> count 2, out 83 83            ("SS")
  233  full_index -1, in run 1, stride 1  -> 233 - 32 =  201
  912  full_index 3   -> count 3, out 921 776 769

  put-utf8: 65, 83 and 83 are one byte each; the rest are under 0x800, so two:
    201 -> 0xC3=195, 0x89=137
    921 -> 0xCE=206, 0x99=153
    776 -> 0xCC=204, 0x88=136
    769 -> 0xCC=204, 0x81=129
  bytes 65 83 83 195 137 206 153 204 136 204 129, folded to
    55546609842069635

DOWNCASING. lo = [[65 90 32 1]] -- an ASCII-only table -- and `full_index`
answers -1 for every code point, so all four pass through unchanged and this
arm walks `case-map` only.

  bytes 97 195 159 195 169 206 144   (223 -> 0xC3 0x9F, 233 -> 0xC3 0xA9,
                                      912 -> 0xCE 0x90)
  folded: 97 -> 3202 -> 99421 -> 3082246 -> 95549795 -> 2962043851 ->
          91823359525

THE DERIVATION WAS CHECKED AGAINST THE PREVIOUS ONE. The model above was
written as a script, run against the OLD fixture first, and reproduced
`65997091 95549795 8` exactly before it was trusted for the new numbers. A
derivation that has never produced a known answer is a guess with arithmetic
in it.

THE TWO ANSWERS MUST DIFFER, and they differ in the FIRST byte and the last:
that is what makes this pair a check rather than a coincidence. A
`change-case` that ignored its `up` flag would print the same number twice.
The subject deliberately holds two code points that are above 127 -- the Rust
this replaced answered `nil` for any such string, "which is not a terse answer
but a wrong one".

steps=10. `charge-checked` is called ONCE per conversion with `n + 1` where n
is the CODE-POINT count: 4 + 1 = 5, twice. Not per byte and not per output --
the upcased arm emits eleven bytes from four code points, so a charge that
followed the output would print something larger here. The point recorded in
the source is that charging per iteration billed 48097 steps past an exhausted
budget, because billing is not bounding. A source that moved the charge inside
the loop would print 8.

THE GAP THIS CLOSED. The `--rust` section was headed "'a-sharp-s' upcased: 'a'
by delta, sharp s by a FULL mapping to two code points" and NO FULL MAPPING
HAPPENED: `full_index` returned -1 unconditionally, so `fx < 0` on every code
point and the whole `case-full-at` branch -- the inner loop, the `cp-unsigned`
conversions, the one-to-many expansion -- was never entered. Sharp s came out
unchanged at 223, which the old numbers showed to anyone who checked them
against the heading.

Two real rows now sit in CASE_FULL, copied from `casetable.kin`'s own `:data`:
row 0, sharp s -> 83 83 with count 2, and row 3, U+0390 -> 921 776 769 with
count 3. BOTH COUNTS ARE THERE ON PURPOSE. A single count could not distinguish
a source that read the count from the wrong field from one that read it right,
and an expansion of exactly two cannot tell `k + 2` from anything that happens
to coincide at two.

PROVED BOTH WAYS:

  new fixture, (+ k 2) -> (+ k 1)                  fold changes, caught
  new fixture, count field 1 -> field 0            CRASHES, caught -- field 0
                                                   is the code point 223, so
                                                   the inner loop runs 223
                                                   times and indexes past the
                                                   515-long array
  OLD fixture, EITHER mutation                     PASSES

The old fixture catching neither is the evidence that the gap was real rather
than a reading of the source, and it is the bar the remaining entries in
`DECISIONS.md#kin-probes-assert-a-value` have to clear.
